  "self_load_only": true,
  "description": "bigville R27 (block 315000): SENTENCING BY COLLAPSE, BOUNDED BY LAW. On a GUILTY verdict the council DECIDES the custodial term by collapse -- but the law limits it to a statutory [min_term,max_term]. A SentenceLaw{offence,min_term,max_term,status} lives in the LawBook (amendable by the council). sn_sentence: the council's DESIRED severity = charge.base_days + (condemn_count - threshold) (how hard it condemned beyond bare guilt); the term = Attr(Argmax over SentenceLevel candidates valued by IfThenElse(min<=days<=max, -(days-desired)^2, -inf), 'days') -- the Argmax may only pick a level INSIDE the legal range, and picks the admissible level nearest desired. THE LAW IS THE ADMISSIBLE SET: desired above the ceiling -> max_term; below the floor -> min_term. The chosen term is written to charge.jail_term; jl_imprison (314000) then gaols for exactly that. Acquittal -> no term. Amend max_term -> the ceiling moves (real law, not a constant).",
